          "doc": "AMS1117 1A Low Dropout Voltage Regulator",
          "at": "Electrical Characteristics, AMS1117-5.0 output voltage typical at VIN = 6.5 V and TJ = +25 C. The section is at IOUT = 0 unless a row says otherwise. The row's limits at 25 C are 4.925 V to 5.075 V.",
          "basis": "typical"
        }
      }
    },
    "line_regulation": {
      "value": 4.761904761904762e-05,
      "unit": "1",
      "source": {
        "closed_form": {
          "note": "0.5 mV typical line regulation of the AMS1117-5.0 at TJ = +25 C, divided by 10.5 V. The span is (VIN - VOUT) from 1.5 V to 12 V. The maximum on that row is 10 mV."
        }
      }
    },
    "output_resistance": {
      "value": 0.00625,
      "unit": "ohm",
      "source": {
        "closed_form": {
          "note": "5 mV typical load regulation of the AMS1117-5.0 at VIN = 6.5 V, IOUT from 0 to 0.8 A, TJ = +25 C, divided by 0.8 A. The maximum on that row is 20 mV."
        }
      }
    },
    "dropout_voltage": {
      "value": 1.0992,
      "unit": "V",
      "source": {
        "closed_form": {
          "note": "1.1 V typical dropout at 0.8 A, minus 0.001 ohm times 0.8 A, so the drop is 1.1 V at that current. The condition is a 1 percent fall in VOUT. The maximum on the row is 1.3 V. The sheet states that one current."
        }
      }
    },
    "dropout_resistance": {
      "value": 0.001,
      "unit": "ohm",
      "source": {
        "closed_form": {
          "note": "0.001 ohm, so the drop stays 1.1 V at 0.8 A and the resistance stays positive. The sheet states dropout at that one current. The description says the drop decreases at lower load currents, and Note 4 says it is higher above 0.8 A. Neither slope is on the sheet."
        }
      }
    },
    "current_limit": {
      "value": 1.1,
      "unit": "A",
      "source": {
        "datasheet": {
          "doc": "AMS1117 1A Low Dropout Voltage Regulator",
          "at": "Current Limit typical, 1100 mA, at (VIN - VOUT) = 1.5 V, for the fixed versions. The minimum on that row is 900 mA and the maximum is 1500 mA.",
          "basis": "typical"
        }
      }
    },
    "quiescent_current": {
      "value": 0.005,
      "unit": "A",
      "source": {
        "datasheet": {
          "doc": "AMS1117 1A Low Dropout Voltage Regulator",
          "at": "Quiescent Current typical, 5 mA, for the fixed versions. The maximum on that row is 11 mA. The table's condition is (VIN - VOUT) = 1.5 V, and the section is at IOUT = 0 unless a row says otherwise.",
          "basis": "typical"
        }
      }
    },
    "ground_current_ratio": {
      "value": 0,
      "unit": "1",
      "source": {
        "closed_form": {
          "note": "The quiescent-current row gives no load term, so the model holds the ground current at 5 mA while the input is up."
        }
      }
    },
    "ratings": {
      "current": {
        "value": 1.0,
        "unit": "A",
        "basis": "peak",
        "source": {
          "datasheet": {
            "doc": "AMS1117 1A Low Dropout Voltage Regulator",
            "at": "Features, output current of 1 A. The load-regulation and dropout rows stop at 0.8 A, and Note 4 says dropout above 0.8 A is higher.",
